I have compiled both NH3.0j and NH3.1 on a 486DX/33, 4 megs ram.

I compiled 3.0j with MSC 7.0, and it took about 3 hours, because it
apparently compiled each source file 3 times, each time with a
different define on the command line.

NH3.1 took me an hour with djgpp. 

I have tried 3.1 compiled with both MSC (the official one from
wuarchive) and mine with gcc, and although gcc's is much faster
(actually, it doesn't really matter with a 486), I use the official
one, because I can't run the gcc binary from Windows, and I can't
escape to a shell from DOS.

